From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Hardware bitmaps become ordinary bitmaps without a GPU

Test V32, reported by the user: long-pressing an application icon makes
Launcher3 stop, repeatedly.

  java.lang.IllegalStateException: Software rendering doesn't support hardware bitmaps
      at android.graphics.BaseCanvas.throwIfHwBitmapInSwMode
      at com.android.launcher3.graphics.ShadowDrawable.draw

Launcher3 caches the shadowed drop-target icons as Bitmap.Config.HARDWARE.
On PW3 every window is drawn by the software canvas (0006), which cannot
draw such a bitmap, and creating one goes through CPU-emulated GLES. Any
application may ask for hardware bitmaps (Bitmap.copy, BitmapFactory with
inPreferredConfig, BitmapRegionDecoder); all of these end in
Bitmap::allocateHardwareBitmap(), which now returns an immutable copy in
ordinary memory when the software canvas is selected.

--- a/libs/hwui/hwui/Bitmap.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/hwui/Bitmap.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 
 #include <log/log.h>
 #include <cutils/ashmem.h>
+#include <cutils/properties.h>
 
 #include <private/gui/ComposerService.h>
 #include <binder/IServiceManager.h>
@@ -84,7 +85,33 @@
     return sk_sp<Bitmap>(new Bitmap(addr, size, info, rowBytes));
 }
 
+// PW3: there is no GPU and every window is drawn by the software canvas (the
+// same properties as in ActivityThread). That canvas refuses hardware bitmaps
+// ("Software rendering doesn't support hardware bitmaps": Launcher3 crashed
+// on Test V32 as soon as a drag showed its drop targets), and creating one
+// would upload a texture through CPU-emulated GLES.
+static bool softwareCanvasOnly() {
+    static const bool only = property_get_bool("debug.pw3.software_canvas",
+            property_get_bool("ro.pw3.software_canvas", false));
+    return only;
+}
+
 sk_sp<Bitmap> Bitmap::allocateHardwareBitmap(SkBitmap& bitmap) {
+    if (softwareCanvasOnly()) {
+        // An immutable copy in ordinary memory instead. It reports its real
+        // config, so callers that asked for Config.HARDWARE can draw it.
+        sk_sp<Bitmap> copy = allocateHeapBitmap(bitmap.info());
+        if (!copy) {
+            return nullptr;
+        }
+        SkBitmap pixels;
+        copy->getSkBitmap(&pixels);
+        if (!bitmap.readPixels(pixels.info(), pixels.getPixels(), pixels.rowBytes(), 0, 0)) {
+            return nullptr;
+        }
+        copy->setImmutable();
+        return copy;
+    }
     return uirenderer::renderthread::RenderProxy::allocateHardwareBitmap(bitmap);
 }
 
